BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191157@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T190000
SUMMARY:TEDxBoston: Visions of the Next 250 - A First Look
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 1 spot left\
 nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/ev
 ents/191157\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion \nFor 250 years\, Mas
 sachusetts has been a place where bold ideas take root. On June 22nd\, the
  evening before the Visions of the Next 250 gathering at GBH\, we invite m
 embers to a private preview in The Reading Room to explore a more challeng
 ing question: what will the next 250 years look like\, and who is shaping 
 them?\n\nJohn Werner\, venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI c
 olumnist\, will interview four people working at the frontier of science\,
  medicine\, education\, ethics\, and intelligence in the kind of off-the-r
 ecord conversation that needs fewer chairs to go deeper.\n\nTogether\, the
 y will explore some of the defining questions of our time: where machine i
 ntelligence is headed and what it asks of us\; how wearable technology and
  data are transforming our understanding of health\, resilience\, and huma
 n performance\; how society can thoughtfully navigate the ethical challeng
 es that accompany powerful new technologies\; and how education and lifelo
 ng learning must evolve to prepare future generations for a world increasi
 ngly shaped by innovation and artificial intelligence.\n\nSpeakers include
 :\n\nAlham Saadat - Executive Director\, The Innovation Trail of Greater B
 oston\nAlex Wissner-Gross - Investor & Entrepreneur\nEmily Capodilupo - Se
 nior Vice President of Research\, Algorithms\, and Data\, WHOOP\nJoseph Ao
 un - President\, Northeastern University\n\n*This event is complimentary a
 nd reserved for members\, plus one guest. Light bites and refreshments wil
 l be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191157
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-190012@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260623T150000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260623
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260624
SUMMARY:TEDxBoston: Visions of the Next 250
LOCATION:Offsite: GBH Studios
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are
  on Waitlist\nTime: 3 PM – 7 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse
 .com/events/190012\n\nFor 250 years\, Massachusetts has produced the ideas
  that shaped a nation: public education\, the telephone\, the first Americ
 an node of the World Wide Web. The next 250 begin now.\n\nAs part of the s
 tatewide Our America 250 initiative\, join us at GBH for a one-day gatheri
 ng on what comes next. Thirty speakers take the stage in interviews and ta
 lks\, mapping the forces that will define America's next chapter: artifici
 al intelligence\, the future of work\, energy and climate technology\, and
  the reinvention of education.\n\nA preview of featured speakers:\n\nAndre
 w Lau - CEO of Jellyfish\nJoseph Aoun - President of Northeastern Universi
 ty and author of Robot-Proof\nLibby Wayman - Partner at Breakthrough Energ
 y Ventures\nNeil Thompson - Director of MIT FutureTech and Principal Inves
 tigator at MIT's Initiative on the Digital Economy\n\nCurated and moderate
 d by John Werner\, venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI colum
 nist. Every talk is recorded as a living time capsule\, a message to the g
 enerations who will open it on the road to America's 500th.\n\nPlease look
  forward to additional details regarding related Programming hosted at The
  'Quin on June 22nd. More information to follow.\n\n*This event is complim
 entary and reserved for members\, plus one guest.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/190012
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
